// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO6 tagged "button" - confirmed onboard PWR (power)
// side button. Vendor firmware source (waveshareteam/ESP32-S3-Touch-
// LCD-1.46 GitHub repo, example/Arduino-3.1.1/examples/LVGL_Arduino/
// PWR_Key.h) defines PWR_KEY_Input_PIN = GPIO6, read via digitalRead()
// as a momentary pushbutton (pinMode INPUT; pressed = LOW). GPIO7
// (PWR_Control_PIN) is the associated power-hold/enable output line,
// not a button or LED, and is left untagged. No onboard BOOT-button
// GPIO or user-controllable LED/NeoPixel could be confirmed from vendor
// sources - see boardsDetails notes.txt for details.
